{"nodes": [{"id": "information_sppr_methods_summary", "label": "SPPR Calculation Methods Reference (SPPR_Methods.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "information_sppr_methods_sppr", "label": "SPPR (Specific Primary Production Required)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "information_sppr_methods_te", "label": "Transfer Efficiency (TE) and TE_option", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "information_sppr_methods_tl", "label": "Trophic Level (TL)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "information_sppr_methods_dc_matrix", "label": "Diet Composition Matrix (DC)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "information_sppr_methods_nullspace_formulation", "label": "Nullspace Fixed-Point Formulation (x = A\u00b7x, nullspace of L = A \u2212 I)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The SPPR vector is a fixed point of the per-edge weight matrix A (eigenvalue 1), so it lives in the nullspace of L = A \u2212 I; solving in closed form automatically sums all pathways and all cycles (the geometric series I + A + A\u00b2 + \u2026), which path enumeration struggles to do exactly."}, {"id": "information_sppr_methods_leontief_io", "label": "Leontief Input-Output Formulation ((I \u2212 A)\u207b\u00b9)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "information_sppr_methods_detritus_recycling", "label": "Detritus Recycling Coupled System ((I \u2212 B)x = c)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Detritus is not a true primary source: its SPPR value depends on the SPPR of everything dying into it, which itself depends partly on detritus's own value, producing a self-consistency fixed point. With multiple pools this becomes a linear system (I\u2212B)x=c, where B is the recycling coupling traced through the living nullspace and back down through mortality/egestion; solved because a single scalar or matrix solve closes the death\u2192detritus\u2192consumption\u2192death loop exactly rather than approximating it."}, {"id": "information_sppr_methods_spectral_radius_condition", "label": "Spectral Radius Convergence Condition (b = \u03c1(B) < 1, Perron\u2013Frobenius)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "B is entrywise non-negative, so by Perron\u2013Frobenius (I\u2212B)\u207b\u00b9 \u2265 0 iff b < 1: only then is a finite non-negative solution guaranteed for every admissible c. b \u2265 1 means recycling regenerates at least as much detritus as it consumes each pass, so the Neumann series diverges; this is why det_collapse_mode offers 'auto'/'always' pooling as a stabilizing fallback rather than trusting the direct solve unconditionally."}, {"id": "information_sppr_methods_jensen_correction", "label": "monte_carlo_SPPR Jensen's-Inequality Correction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SPPR is a function of 1/TE, which is convex, so by Jensen's inequality E[1/TE] \u2265 1/E[TE], hence E[SPPR(TE)] \u2265 SPPR(E[TE]): solving once at the mean TE systematically underestimates expected PPR because it ignores the extra requirement contributed by the low-TE tail. monte_carlo_SPPR exists specifically to recover the unbiased (higher) expectation by resampling TE and averaging, not merely to produce an error bar."}, {"id": "information_sppr_methods_gamma_sampling", "label": "Gamma-Distribution TE Resampling", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TE must stay strictly positive because 1/TE diverges near zero and negative TE is meaningless, so each per-group TE is drawn from a Gamma(alpha, theta) distribution parameterized to preserve the model mean and a specified coefficient of variation \u2014 a symmetric normal would be wrong here. Non-positive model TEs are pinned rather than sampled, since gamma requires a strictly positive scale."}, {"id": "information_sppr_methods_pauly_christensen_1986", "label": "Pauly & Christensen (1986)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "information_sppr_methods_christensen_pauly_1995", "label": "Christensen & Pauly (1995)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "information_sppr_methods_summary", "target": "information_sppr_methods_sppr", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "information_sppr_methods_sppr", "target": "information_sppr_methods_te", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "information_sppr_methods_sppr", "target": "information_sppr_methods_tl", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "information_sppr_methods_te", "target": "information_sppr_methods_dc_matrix", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pprestimation_pprcalculator_sppr_1986", "target": "information_sppr_methods_pauly_christensen_1986", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pprestimation_pprcalculator_sppr_1995", "target": "information_sppr_methods_christensen_pauly_1995", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pprestimation_pprcalculator_sppr_1995_tl_fix", "target": "pprestimation_pprcalculator_sppr_1995", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PPREstimation/information/SPPR_Methods.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "ppres